      <!-- ─── SECTION 3 ─── -->
      <section id="two-component">
        <h2>Two-Component Polyurethane Sealant Formulation</h2>

        <p>
          Where the 1K moisture-cure mechanism imposes humidity-dependent cure rates and CO₂ blistering risks, two-component polyurethane systems resolve these constraints by separating the curing chemistry into two shelf-stable components that react only when mixed. Part A contains the NCO-terminated prepolymer formulated with plasticisers, stabilisers, and fillers. Part B contains the curative package: a blend of polyol and/or amine crosslinker, organotin or tertiary amine catalyst, pigment paste, and filler. When combined at the specified mix ratio (typically 3:1 to 5:1 Part A:Part B by volume), Part A isocyanate groups react with Part B hydroxyl and amine groups directly — without moisture involvement — to form urethane and urea crosslinks rapidly and predictably.
        </p>

        <p>
          Pot life — the working time after mixing — is a critical 2K formulation parameter, governing how much time the applicator has to fill, tool, and finish the joint before gelation begins. Construction-grade 2K PU sealants are typically formulated for 30–90 minutes pot life. Full surface cure (tack-free) is reached in 2–8 hours at 23°C; full mechanical properties develop within 24–72 hours, considerably faster than the 7-day cure of 1K systems. This makes 2K systems the preferred choice for production environments and for winter construction work where low humidity or cold temperatures would make 1K cure unreliable. A detailed comparison with the competing silicone sealant chemistry — which offers superior UV stability but cannot be overpainted — is available in our guide to <a href="/silicone-sealants-types-grades-applications" target="_top">silicone sealant types, grades, and applications</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Property</th>
                <th>1K Moisture-Cure PU</th>
                <th>2K Chemical-Cure PU</th>
